  "query_preview": "..Water vapor imagery this morning showed shortwave\nridge axis over eastern Arizona and upper level trof along the\nwest coast. High clouds will be on the increase as the day \nprogresses, becoming thick at times this afternoon/evening.\nThe southern end of this west coast upper trof will break off \nlater today and develop into a closed low tonight over northern \nBaja and dig toward the Baja tip on Thursday with upper level \nridge edging in across the state through Friday and hanging \naround into the weekend. Daily high temperatures through the\nweekend will gradually warm each day.\n\nMonday: November closes out on a slightly cooler note.\n\nPattern change during the remainder of next week as ensembles \nshow several Pacific trofs moving thru the desert southwest \nbringing enhanced chances of precipitation, including high \nelevation mountain snow.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Wed Dec 2 to Mon Dec 7)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (35%-39%)\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal (45%)",
